    <tags>aws cli saml saml2aws sso entra-id cross-platform foss</tags>
    <summary>AWS credentials from a browser-based SAML sign-in.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[samlgate is a browser-based alternative to `saml2aws login`.

It opens your IdP sign-in (Microsoft Entra ID, Okta, Google Workspace, ...) in Microsoft Edge or another installed
Chromium browser using a dedicated persistent profile, captures the SAML assertion on its way to AWS, exchanges it
for temporary credentials with STS, and writes them to `~/.aws/credentials` in the same format saml2aws uses.

- Reads compatible account settings from `~/.saml2aws`
- Supports `credential_process` and `exec`
- No Playwright or browser-driver downloads; a single native executable

Requires Microsoft Edge (included with Windows), Google Chrome, Brave, Chromium or Whale.

Uninstalling the package removes `samlgate.exe` only. `~/.samlgate`, `~/.aws/credentials` and the dedicated browser
profile are left in place.
]]></description>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
